# A komi chosen after the board appears has to reach the engines. It used to
# ride on the sync that ran at the first move; since that sync moved to the
# moment the board changes (ADR-0008), a later komi stayed in the model alone,
# and the engines played and scored the game with the one they were given at
# the new game.
#
# Empty board, two passes: the mock scores area minus komi, so who won says
# which komi it was told. A reverse komi makes Black the winner; the stale 6.5
# would make it White.

new_game 9
wait_idle
switch_player black human
switch_player white human
wait_idle
expect komi 6.5

komi -3.5
wait_idle
expect komi -3.5

pass
wait_until move_count >= 1
pass
wait_until has_result true
wait_idle
expect msg black_won
expect result black_won
